{{also|Tirade}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
/ˈtaɪreɪd/
*: {{rhymes|eɪd}}

=== Etymology ===
From the French:  Lit. a stretch; a continuous pulling; Italian  tirata/ tirato,  past participle of tirare  "to draw, pull, fire (a shot)"

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A long, angry, [[tendentious]], accusative or [[violent]] [[speech]]; a [[diatribe]]
# A section of [[verse]] concerning a single [[theme]]; a [[laisse]]
# A long section of a written work.
====Synonyms====
* {{sense|speech}} [[diatribe]]
* {{sense|section of verse}} [[laisse]]
* harangue
* diatribe
* denunciation
* See also [[Wikisaurus:diatribe]]

